{
  "id": "beastmaster",
  "name": "Beastmaster",
  "version": "1.16.1",
  "description": "A Beastmaster class: tame wild wolves, boars, sabretooths and hounds (beat them down or feed them bait), and bears, aurochs and snakes with the EMF creature packs (a wild snake is now and then a rare crimson, golden king or albino one, with a bonus for whoever slays it), keep up to 8 in your collection, call as many to fight beside you as your active slots (1 at the start, up to 4 with your level), and choose them at a stable (the game's animal bed in your base, or the Stable or Large Stable of the beasts pack, crafted at the Workbench: press E at it). In a Large Stable the beasts you left at home walk about, lie down, sleep through the night, and can be petted (E Pet: a loyalty point once a game day). Loyal beasts earn talent points (Strength, Toughness, Swiftness, Second Wind, Ambush, Guard, Menace, Taunt), spent on each beast's tab of the Beasts window (it shows the beast slowly turning, drawn from your own game). Monsters split between you and your beasts: a tank draws half of them. Markers (off at the start): your beasts' names over their heads and on the map, and the stables on the map. They follow you, come back when far away, pass the time while you stand still (lie down, sit by a fire, watch a villager, keep watch at night), and are kept with the world. Hold F3 for the beast wheel. Players who join with EMF and Beastmaster switched on in their own game get the window, the wheel and the beast line too (others type /beastmaster in the chat), and the stables their games see count on a dedicated server. Host or dedicated server. Installed switched off.",
  "authors": ["EMF contributors"],
  "enabled": false,
  "emf": 14,
  "side": "server",
  "main": "main.lua",
  "depends": {"lua": ">=1.25"},
